{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1410868-fellow-writers-has-exalted-s-world-influenced-your-worlds-at-all","id":1410868,"title":"Fellow writers, has Exalted's world influenced your worlds at all?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-28T12:47:46-07:00","id":1410868,"title":"Fellow writers, has Exalted's world influenced your worlds at all?","content":"It has for mine! I love Creation. Perhaps a bit too much. Specifically, in one world I'm working on, the whole structure of the divine sphere is very similar, with Terrestrials living on the mortal plane and Celestials living in a huge heavenly city and organized into an absolute travesty of a bureaucracy. In fact I think I plagiarize Exalted a bit too much here, and I'm constantly taxing my brain to use Exalted's ideas in a unique and different way, but the main differences for now are:<br /> <br /> -Whoever the equivalent to Primordials are in this world (I intentionally go into very little detail, as it's not important), they left without a trace. There are no direct equivalents to Yozis or the Neverborn or anything of that.<br /> <br /> -The gods had a large war early on, but it was a civil war between gods who wanted absolute control over fate and their domains and gods who wanted to bureaucratically oversee their domains and &quot;automate&quot; the basic running of reality; the first group lost and were called the Asura. They ran away to the world of spirits (<i>roughly </i>the Wyld, but not really), though some were taken as prisoners. They also secretly taught humanity how to wield magic and spiritual power for their own before they left.<br /> <br /> -There is no equivalent to the Loom of Fate--instead, at the center of Heaven lies a huge &quot;engine of reality&quot; that automates the running of the world, as long as the gods feed data into it. This doesn't control fate, it's basically just what lets physics exist (I know the LoF <i>also</i> does that, but this thing can't be studied for insights into the future). The entire reason for the divine civil war was the Asura objecting to the idea that gods wouldn't have absolute despotic power over their domains and instead would become lazy bureaucrats (it should be noted that most of the Asura were bourgeois gods of things like the sun and moon, who barely had to do anything and therefore didn't understand why gods who had to do things like micromanage <i>every single weather pattern on the planet</i> would want to automate their jobs).<br /> <br /> -There is no equivalent to the Sidereals (in fact there are no equivalents to Exalts at all, as humans can just grind and train their way to power and there aren't distinct &quot;types&quot; of superpowered humans); there are humans in Heaven, but they are basically an entire <i>race</i> of janitors, street cleaners, and whatever else jobs the gods of Heaven broadly consider beneath them. Despite this, they still tend to treat Terrestrial gods with classist contempt.<br /> <br /> Still, the main themes, that is the divine race being split between classist out-of-touch bluebloods in their cushy country club and beleagered proles who are shackled to a bureaucracy that treats them as expendable hillbilly bumpkins at <i>best</i>, affords them no voice, and barely even lets them enter the place they are supposedly employed to with zero liberty in the matter, are there.<br /> <br /> I'm currently working on making this different to Exalted's paradigm in some ways. It feels too close for its own good. I might bring in some influence from Autochthonia, but a lot of that world doesn't make sense when applied to effectively immortal beings who have no need to reproduce or give prayers to anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 08-28-2020, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T13:13:47-07:00","id":1410871,"title":"","content":"My first full D&amp;D campaign was Exalted-inspired. The divine pantheon were clear Incarnae-equivalents and the campaign\u2019s premise was based on the chaos caused by resurrection magic in a world with strict reincarnation. The PCs were resurrected ancient heroes, which ripped their souls out of their modern incarnations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T23:26:06-07:00","id":1410954,"title":"","content":"I just drop the pretense and write Exalted fanfiction!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T01:20:49-07:00","id":1411055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1410868-fellow-writers-has-exalted-s-world-influenced-your-worlds-at-all?p=1410954#post1410954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just drop the pretense and write Exalted fanfiction!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! Hello, my newfound friend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T20:48:43-07:00","id":1411161,"title":"","content":"Great to meet you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T16:06:52-07:00","id":1411268,"title":"","content":"I have permanently been inspired by Exalted uses of Stunts in every edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T13:35:15-07:00","id":1411548,"title":"","content":"Well with enough thought I've managed to make things a bit more unique...by cribbing from Autochthonia. Now Celestial gods comprise both the Exalted idea of them and a bunch of heavenly gods whose jobs are maintenance of this reality engine I've mentioned in a way similar to the Populat in Autothchonia.<br /> <br /> Unlike Yu-Shan, prayer from mortals isn't split into two types and and in fact forms in Heaven in the form of various divine metals, ores, or even strange things like perfectly pure lakes of gold and trees of silver which grow jade apples according to worryingly inscrutable mechanisms, and whereas Yu-Shan is an entire city-continent, Heaven in this setting is actually full of untamed countryside and small towns and cities which mostly manufacture stuff for this reality engine which is then shipped to Olympus (the central city of Heaven) for use in making sure reality, you know, works. A lot of the prayer is specifically melted down and purified into the closest equivalent of Ambrosia and Quintessence. This stuff isn't as good as those though, so the gods cannot just willy-nilly will whatever they want into existence like Exalted's gods can.<br /> <br /> Thus the Exalted split of Terrestrial and Celestial is a bit more complicated--it still exists, but many of Heaven's gods are beleaguered proles and rural workers whose experience of Heaven's supposedly infinite splendor is working long shifts and experiencing little in the way of spiritual enlightenment--the Exalted style of Celestial ('bougie layabout who spends more time getting into random petty wankery than actual working&quot;) is only for the upper class neoliberals of Heaven. Less ignorant Terrestrials will often refer to these specific bourgeoisie gods as &quot;Olympians&quot; to distinguish them from the proles whose lives are only marginally better than their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T14:44:08-07:00","id":1411568,"title":"","content":"I can neither confirm nor deny that the five castes of the goddess of light's holy city of Lampide have anything to do with the five Solar Castes. I also cannot confirm or deny that the Kunai - ninjas that make use of an esoteric calligraphy based around the true names of all things - were in any way inspired by the concept of He Who Bleeds and/or Wordblood from Lunar Quest. Nor the idea that all magical power flows from the gods in some form or another (less sure about this one as it makes aforementioned ninjas a bit iffy), nor even the presence of a heavily matriarchal and authoritarian warrior society in the mountains that once held a vast empire.<br /> <br /> (okay to be fair that last one draws a lot more on the Amazons, Rome, and a dash of Warhammer 40k)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T05:01:23-07:00","id":1411774,"title":"","content":"My sci-fi game Machineborn started out as an Exalted Shard before I rewrote it as a stand-alone game. The setting was originally inspired by Exalted (because it was a Shard) but I've removed all of the blatant references since. There are still some references here and there, though, and much of the setting framework is still (albeit loosely) inspired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}